## Outside a fragment

Clauses with a function symbol have infinitely many ground instances. Expected: **Inappropriate**, with the statement and the reason; the outcome has no output.

<!-- livebook:{"attrs":"eyJlbmdpbmUiOiJncm91bmQiLCJpbnB1dCI6bnVsbCwibGFuZ3VhZ2UiOiJ0cHRwIiwib3B0aW9ucyI6e30sInJvbGVzIjp7fSwic291cmNlIjoiY25mKG51bWJlcnMsIGF4aW9tLCBuYXQoemVybykpLlxuY25mKHN1Y2Nlc3NvciwgYXhpb20sIG5hdChzKFgpKSB8IH4gbmF0KFgpKS5cbiIsInZhcmlhYmxlIjoibm90X2dyb3VuZCJ9","chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.KinoLoge.Cell","livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
not_ground =
  Loge.run!(
    Loge.Tptp.Engines.Ground,
    "cnf(numbers, axiom, nat(zero)).\ncnf(successor, axiom, nat(s(X)) | ~ nat(X)).\n",
    []
  )
```

A cell that takes such an outcome as its input does not run on nothing: it stops with the same reasons.

```elixir
try do
  Loge.run!(Loge.Tptp.Engines.Dimacs, not_ground, [])
rescue
  error in ArgumentError -> Kino.Markdown.new("```\n" <> Exception.message(error) <> "\n```")
end
```

## How the translations are checked

`loge_verification` runs every edge above on generated inputs and compares what a
solver says about the input with what another says about the output: clasp, clingo,
SWI-Prolog and egglog always, z3 and Vampire when installed. From that directory:
`mix test`, or `mix test --include z3 --include vampire`.
